/-!
# Free additive convolution of compactly supported laws on `ℝ`

Given compactly supported probability measures `μ` and `ν` on `ℝ`, one realizes them simultaneously
as the laws of freely independent bounded selfadjoint operators `a` and `b` in the reduced C⋆-free
product of `C(μ.support, ℂ)` and `C(ν.support, ℂ)` represented on its GNS Hilbert space (and hence
also in the concrete von Neumann algebras generated by the factor representations). The *free
additive convolution* `μ.freeConv ν` (traditionally written `μ ⊞ ν`) is defined as the law of
`a + b`; outside compactly supported probability measures it takes the junk value `0`.

Because the joint algebraic distribution of a freely independent family is determined by its
one-variable power moments
(`TauCeti.IsFreelyIndependentElements.jointDistribution_eq_of_forall_pow`) and compactly supported
laws on `ℝ` are determined by their moments (`PositiveLinearMap.law_eq_law_iff_forall_apply_pow`),
the law of `∑ i ∈ s, a i` for any freely independent family of selfadjoint elements in any
C⋆-probability space depends only on the marginal laws `φ.law (a i)`. In particular,
`φ.law (a + b) = (φ.law a).freeConv (φ.law b)` holds in every C⋆-probability space and, via weak
operator closure, for freely independent von Neumann subalgebras under WOT-continuous states.

## Main definitions

* `MeasureTheory.Measure.freeConv μ ν` — the free additive convolution of two Borel measures on
  `ℝ`, defined as the law of `a + b` in a Hilbert-space reduced C⋆-free product realization when
  `μ` and `ν` are compactly supported probability measures, and `0` otherwise.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.ReducedFreeProduct.law_factor_innerPositiveLinearMap_vacuum` and
  `TauCeti.ReducedFreeProduct.isFreelyIndependent_vonNeumannAlgebraAdjoin_factor` — law
  compatibility and von Neumann algebra freeness for reduced C⋆-free products on their GNS Hilbert
  space.
* `TauCeti.exists_hilbert_isFreelyIndependent_law_eq` — simultaneous realization of any indexed
  family of compactly supported probability measures on `ℝ` by freely independent norm-closed
  `⋆`-subalgebras and freely independent von Neumann subalgebras on a Hilbert space with a unit
  vector state, preserving Loewner interval bounds from the supports.
* `TauCeti.IsFreelyIndependentElements.law_sum_congr` and
  `TauCeti.IsFreelyIndependent.law_sum_congr` — realization independence of the law of a finite sum
  of freely independent selfadjoint elements, proved directly from moment determinacy.
* `TauCeti.IsFreelyIndependent.law_add`, `TauCeti.IsFreelyIndependentElements.law_add`, and
  `TauCeti.IsFreelyIndependent.law_add_of_mem_vonNeumannAlgebraAdjoin` — in any C⋆- or concrete
  von Neumann realization, the law of `a + b` is `(φ.law a).freeConv (φ.law b)`.
* `MeasureTheory.Measure.rSeries_freeConv` and `MeasureTheory.Measure.freeCumulant_freeConv` —
  additivity of the formal R-series and of the free cumulants under `freeConv`.
* `MeasureTheory.Measure.freeConv_comm`, `MeasureTheory.Measure.freeConv_assoc`,
  `MeasureTheory.Measure.freeConv_dirac`, `MeasureTheory.Measure.freeConv_dirac_zero`, and
  `MeasureTheory.Measure.dirac_zero_freeConv` — commutativity, associativity, and Dirac translation
  and identity laws.
* `MeasureTheory.Measure.freeConv_map_affine`, `MeasureTheory.Measure.freeConv_map_mul_left`,
  `MeasureTheory.Measure.freeConv_map_add_right`, and `MeasureTheory.Measure.freeConv_map_neg` —
  compatibility with real affine pushforwards.
* `MeasureTheory.Measure.support_freeConv_subset_Iic`,
  `MeasureTheory.Measure.support_freeConv_subset_Ici`,
  `MeasureTheory.Measure.support_freeConv_subset_Icc`,
  `MeasureTheory.Measure.support_freeConv_subset_closedBall`, and
  `MeasureTheory.Measure.support_freeConv_subset_Icc_sInf_sSup` — topological support bounds.

## References

* D. V. Voiculescu, *Addition of certain noncommuting random variables*, J. Funct. Anal. 66 (1986),
  323–346.
* D. V. Voiculescu, K. J. Dykema, A. Nica, *Free Random Variables*, CRM Monograph Ser. 1, Amer.
  Math. Soc. (1992), §3.2.
* A. Nica, R. Speicher, *Lectures on the Combinatorics of Free Probability*, London Math. Soc.
  Lecture Note Ser. 335, Cambridge University Press (2006), Lecture 12.
-/

